node action: one row - uses, sha, action.yml, the raw-byte digest, node24, no nested, no image
CRLF metadata: the digest covers the raw bytes, CRs kept (never the LF-folded text)
an action under a path: metadata_file is the path at the pin (`sub/dir/action.yml`)
action.yml 404 -> the action.yaml fallback is read and named in metadata_file
action.yml and action.yaml both 404 -> refused, naming both
an HTTP status other than 200/404 -> refused, never read as an absent file
composite with a nested SHA pin -> two rows, the pin in the composite's nested_uses
composite nesting a tag-pinned action -> recorded verbatim, never fetched (leg (12) reds it)
a nested cycle (a -> b -> a) terminates with one row each
nested pins are recorded to any depth (three levels -> three rows)
docker action with a :tag image (scorecard-action v2.4.4's runs: block) -> the image recorded as written
the review surface prints the raw `image:` line, numbered, beside the row's digest
a Dockerfile image: the external FROM refs recorded in order (a stage name and scratch skipped)
a Dockerfile path climbing out of the action (`..`) -> refused
a flow-style `runs: {...}` -> refused
a commented `uses:` step the structural read cannot see -> refused (the token count)
an input named `uses` in a node action -> refused (the token count)
a UTF-8 BOM -> refused by the gate's dialect, naming the file
a lone CR -> refused
bytes that are not UTF-8 -> refused
an unknown `runs.using` -> refused
a duplicate `runs.using` -> refused
no `runs:` block -> refused
a file above the size bound -> refused, never truncated
a local ./ action: the in-tree file's digest, sha empty, metadata_file the in-tree path
a tag-pinned uses and a docker:// uses get no row and no fetch (leg (12) judges them)
the render is byte-identical across two runs and workflow orders, LF only, one final newline
the render parses as TOML: schema_version 1 and the rows sorted by (uses, sha)
--write carries a committed image_exempt_reason over for the same (uses, sha)
--check: a committed file equal to the re-record exits 0, a changed row exits 1
--resolve-images: a 401 -> the anonymous Bearer token -> HEAD manifests/<tag> -> the digest reference
--resolve-images refuses a reference without a registry host or a tag
--resolve-images refuses a reply without a sha256 digest
the real HTTP function refuses a non-https URL
a request's bounds are the pinned 30 s per blocking step and 60 s per attempt (g24-net-retry pins the same)
real_http retries a transient 503 with the policy's pauses (2 s, 4 s), then returns the answer
real_http returns a 404 answer at once (no retry)
real_http refuses a transport failure that outlasts the 300 s retry window
after a request spent the window, the run's next request is not attempted
real_http rides a 302 to the same Location into a 503 outage through the whole 300 s window
real_http rides a 302 to a new Location each time into a 503 outage through the whole 300 s window
real_http ends an attempt with no result inside its wall-clock bound and retries it as a timeout
